 "facts": [
  "Jerome 'Jerry' Jacobson, a former police officer, ran security for Simon Marketing, the company that ran McDonald's game promotions.",
  "He stole high-value winning game pieces and passed them to recruiters, friends and relatives, who claimed the prizes and paid him a share.",
  "An anonymous tip led the FBI to investigate; undercover agents posed as a McDonald's film crew and interviewed a $1 million winner about how he 'found' his piece.",
  "In August 2001, about 100 FBI agents fanned out to make arrests across the country.",
  "More than 50 people were convicted of mail fraud and conspiracy; reported losses range from $13 million (DOJ at arrest) to more than $24 million.",
  "Jacobson was sentenced to about three years in federal prison and ordered to pay $12.5 million in restitution."
 ],
